# peeryard patch ergo/002: MempoolAuditor: rebroadcast a pooled transaction together with its in-pool ancestors
# upstream: ergoplatform/ergo#2573 (proposed); origin, witness and responses in patches.json
commit 7ff544825f6c22bce7ec1e9732b7bcb9f19ea67d
Author: cafebedouin <cafebedouin@gmail.com>
Date:   Fri Oct 16 14:34:19 2026 -0500

    MempoolAuditor: follow data inputs in the rebroadcast ancestor walk
    
    The ancestor walk and the announce check followed inputs only. A pooled transaction that creates a data
    input of a selected transaction was not added to the round, and the reader was announced without it; a peer
    that lacks that transaction does not decline the reader but rejects it (ErgoMemPool.process validates it
    with the data input missing). Treat the creator of a data input as an in-pool parent in the walk, and
    announce a transaction only if its data inputs, like its inputs, are in the state or are created by a
    transaction already announced in this round.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

